  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington had a standout day yesterday\u2014$3,917 revenue on 5 groomer-days, running at $573/groomer against a 30-day baseline of $465. That's 23% above trend and reflects both strong capacity deployment (22 grooms + 5 baths) and disciplined upselling (add-on attach jumped to 63% from 50% last week). Retail nearly tripled to $612, signaling front-of-house momentum. Year-to-date you're up 44% in both revenue and appointments across the portfolio\u2014this is real growth. Be proud of this.\n\nHicksville is the attention item. Yesterday was flat ($1,935), but the deeper issue is capacity starvation: only 3.5 groomer-days scheduled for today and tomorrow (with zero bathers tomorrow). That's structural underutilization. Month-to-date Hicksville is up 88% in revenue but running 14 groomer-days vs 6 last month\u2014you've gained market share, yet productivity per groomer dropped to $383 MTD from $438 last month, suggesting the recent groomer additions are still ramping or scheduling is loose. Core groom revenue yesterday was down 4% week-over-week despite higher transaction count, which hints at mix degradation or capacity constraint forcing lower-value bookings.\n\nCross-store pattern: both locations show upselling strength (add-ons up meaningfully), but Hicksville's groomer scheduling for the next two days is dangerously thin heading into Labor Day weekend. Port Washington's calendar is healthier. You have a $318k reactivation pool at Port Washington and $119k at Hicksville\u2014worth mining before holiday softness sets in.\n\n**Today: Port Washington 4 groomer-days + 8.0h bathers; Hicksville 3 groomer-days + 0.0h bathers. Tomorrow: Port Washington idle, Hicksville 1 groomer-day + 15.0h bathers. Next 7 days: 56 groomer-days scheduled (39 Port, 17 Hicksville) with 76h bather support.**"
